<drawables>
    <!-- Launcher icon at the 40x40 the device's compiler.json asks for. Overrides the
         65x65 in resources/ for the products mapped to this path in the jungle; without a
         native-size source the compiler rescales and warns. -->
    <bitmap id="LauncherIcon" filename="launcher_icon.png"/>

    <!-- The brand mark (source/ui/Brand.mc), 36x22 and FLAT. This directory's audience is
         exactly the thirteen 8 bpp MIP products — both fenix 8 Solars, the whole fenix 7
         family, fr955/fr255/enduro3 — on 240 to 280 px of reflective glass with a 64-entry
         palette. Three things are different about this cut, all of them in
         garmin/tools/make_brand_mark.py: the gradient is a three-step ramp of exact palette
         entries (a smooth one would be dithered into mush at 36 px), those entries avoid
         every collision DesignTokens.mc lists (the brand's own cyan quantises to 0x55AAFF,
         which on 8 bpp is already three tokens at once), and the two water lines are gone —
         at this size they are a 1 px smear that reads as dirt, not as sea. The mark is
         therefore the jibe track and the wing, which is the half of the artwork that carries
         the name. -->
    <bitmap id="BrandMark" filename="brand_mark.png" dithering="none"/>
    <!-- The badge, 26x16 and flat, on the same 64-entry palette. It is the smallest thing
         either screen draws, which is why it is the jibe track and the wing and nothing
         else: at 26 px there is no room for a detail that is not the shape of the name. -->
    <bitmap id="BrandBadge" filename="brand_badge.png" dithering="none"/>
</drawables>
